        "description": "LAMP WITH A HIDDEN FAULT, PARTIALLY OBSERVABLE\n\nOne agent, R, must get the lamp running. The lamp may have a fault.\n\nSkills (one skill per decision cycle):\n  Start(agent, lamp): try to start the lamp. A faulty lamp never starts, and even a\n    healthy one sometimes fails to start. The status is ok if the lamp is running afterwards.\n  Inspect(agent, lamp): look the lamp over. The reading (looks_faulty | looks_fine) is\n    usually, but not always, right about whether it is faulty. Status ok.\n  Repair(agent, lamp): work on the stopped lamp. Repairing sometimes clears a fault and\n    never causes one. Status ok whenever the repair was carried out.\n\nHidden: whether the lamp is faulty is decided at random at the start and never shown directly.\n\nObserved after every skill: whether the lamp is running, the skill's status (ok | fail), and after Inspect the reading.\n\nRewards: -0.01 per cycle, an extra -0.05 per repair, +1 when the lamp runs. Discount 0.95.\n\nThe probabilities are NOT given: model each one as a named parameter.",
